# Keep the Docker build context small and reproducible — mirrors .gitignore,
# plus a few things .gitignore doesn't need to care about (the .git history
# itself, editor state).
#
# Deliberately NOT ignored: checkpoints/, configs/, data/. Those are mounted
# as volumes at `docker run` time (see Makefile's `docker-run` target and
# README's Phase 10 section) rather than baked into the image — a 33M-param
# checkpoint is ~100s of MB, and baking one in would mean rebuilding the
# image every time a different model gets served, defeating the whole point
# of api/main.py already being config/env-var driven about which checkpoint
# to load.

.git/
.gitignore
.dockerignore

.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/

.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

.env
.env.local

checkpoints/
configs/
data/
experiments/

.claude/
*.md
!README.md
